<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43167" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scūtātus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Armed with a</i> scutum (long shield): cohortes,
			* <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 1, 39</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">milites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
					8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">33, 14</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 370</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					6, 211</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scūtāti</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>troops bearing shields</i> (opp. the equites): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quattuor milia scutatorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					28, 2, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> =
			scutarius, II. 2.; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3448</span></i>
			(belonging to A. D. 256).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
